==================================================
PORT PLAN
==================================================
- Backend API: 8000
- Postgres: 5433
- Mobile Metro: 8081
- Frontdesk Metro: 8082

Why:
- Mobile keeps default Metro 8081.
- Frontdesk runs on 8082.
- Sunmi dev client may request 8081, so we reverse device 8081 -> host 8082.

==================================================
PREREQUISITES
==================================================
- Docker Desktop running
- Node and npm installed
- Android platform-tools installed
- Sunmi USB debugging enabled
- Repo root:
  C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip

ADB path used everywhere:
  C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe

==================================================
A) FULL START (FIRST RUN / AFTER RESTART / AFTER OFFLINE)
==================================================
Open 3 terminals.

1) TERMINAL A - BACKEND
  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip
  docker compose up -d postgres backend
  Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:8000/health

Expected:
  {"status":"ok"}


2) TERMINAL B - MOBILE (8081)
  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip\mobile
  npx expo start --host lan --port 8081 --clear


3) TERMINAL C - FRONTDESK + USB (8082)
Set adb vars and recover device:
  $env:ADB_MDNS_OPENSCREEN='0'
  $env:ADB_LIBUSB='0'
  $ADB='C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe'

  taskkill /F /IM adb.exe 2>$null | Out-Null
  Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 700
  & $ADB start-server
  & $ADB reconnect offline
  & $ADB devices -l

Pick ONLINE device serial:
  $SERIAL = (& $ADB devices | Select-String "device$" | ForEach-Object { ($_ -split "`t")[0] } | Select-Object -First 1)
  $SERIAL
  if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($SERIAL)) { throw "No ONLINE adb device found. Fix USB/debugging first." }

Apply reverse map:
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse --remove-all
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse tcp:8081 tcp:8082
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse tcp:8082 tcp:8082
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse tcp:8000 tcp:8000
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse --list

Start Frontdesk Metro:
  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip\frontdesk
  $env:EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL='http://127.0.0.1:8000'
  npx expo start --dev-client --host lan --port 8082 --clear

Relaunch app on Sunmi:
& "C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe" -s "V2A4213923214" shell am force-stop com.takeasip.frontdesk
& "C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe" -s "V2A4213923214" shell monkey -p com.takeasip.frontdesk -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1


If screen is still wrong once:
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL shell pm clear com.takeasip.frontdesk
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL shell monkey -p com.takeasip.frontdesk -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1

One-command alternative (auto recover + relaunch):
  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip\frontdesk
  npm run usb:recover

==================================================
B) QUICK DAILY RUN (NO USB/ADB CHANGES)
==================================================
Use this when:
- Same cable and same PC session
- device state is still "device"
- reverse rules still exist

Quick checks:
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL get-state
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse --list

If state is "device" and reverse list contains:
- tcp:8081 tcp:8082
- tcp:8000 tcp:8000
then only do:

1) Start metros:
  mobile terminal:   npx expo start --host lan --port 8081 --clear
  frontdesk terminal: npx expo start --dev-client --host lan --port 8082 --clear

2) Relaunch frontdesk app:
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL shell am force-stop com.takeasip.frontdesk
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL shell monkey -p com.takeasip.frontdesk -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1

If it disconnects after edits/devtools reload:
  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip\frontdesk
  npm run usb:recover

If still broken once:
  npm run usb:recover:clear

If you have multiple adb installs/devices, force exact values first:
  $env:ADB_PATH='C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe'
  $env:ADB_SERIAL='V2A4213923214'
  npm run usb:recover

==================================================
C) FRONTDESK REBUILD (ONLY WHEN NATIVE CODE CHANGES)
==================================================
Do this only after changes in android native files (printer/beep/module):

  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip\frontdesk
  npx expo run:android

Then relaunch app using monkey command.

