==================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
==================================================
1) "adb.exe: device offline"
- Unplug/replug USB
- Unlock Sunmi screen
- Developer options:
  - Revoke USB debugging authorizations
  - Toggle USB debugging off/on
- USB mode: File Transfer (MTP)
- Accept RSA prompt
- Re-run Section A Terminal C steps

2) "unknown command tcp:8081" or "unknown command am/monkey"
Cause:
- $SERIAL is empty
Fix:
- Print $SERIAL
- Re-run auto-detect serial step

3) "Unable to load script"
- Ensure frontdesk Metro is on 8082 and running
- Ensure reverse exists:
  & $ADB -s $SERIAL reverse --list
- Must include:
  - tcp:8081 tcp:8082
  - tcp:8000 tcp:8000
- Relaunch app
- Fast fix:
    cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip\frontdesk
    npm run usb:recover

4) "Cannot find native module ExpoLocation"
Cause:
- Frontdesk loaded wrong bundle
Fix:
  taskkill /F /IM node.exe 2>$null | Out-Null
  Start only:
  - mobile on 8081 from mobile folder
  - frontdesk on 8082 from frontdesk folder
  Re-apply reverse and relaunch app

5) OTP send fails
- Check backend health on http://localhost:8000/health
- Ensure frontdesk env:
  EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
- Ensure reverse tcp:8000 tcp:8000 exists

==================================================
STOP EVERYTHING
==================================================
- Stop Metro terminals with Ctrl+C
- Stop backend:
  cd C:\Users\user\Take-A-Sip\Take-A-Sip
  docker compose down
